<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="ARM:LE:32:v8:default">
<!--
    kuna: a 64-bit return whose high word is computed from the low word, or
    whose low word is the function's argument left in its register, returns
    all eight bytes, not void.

    Stage / sub-stage: P4 return recovery, the output trials of the
    function's own RETURN (ActionReturnRecovery, p4_calls/kuna_retcallhalf.rs),
    and the late pair repair (p4_calls/kuna_returnuncomputed.rs).
    A strict fix: no option.

    Source (clang -target arm-linux-gnueabi -O2, bytes verbatim below; kc0
    is clang -O0 of kc, and the last seven functions are hand-written
    controls):

        typedef unsigned long long u64;
        typedef long long s64;
        s64 sx(int a) { return a + 3; }
        u64 zx(unsigned a) { return a; }
        s64 sxa(int a) { return a; }
        u64 kc(unsigned a) { return a | (5ULL << 32); }
        u64 dupc(unsigned a) { unsigned x = a + 1; return ((u64)x << 32) | x; }
        s64 sxsel(int a, int b) { return a > b ? a : b; }

        div7:   asr r1,r0,#2; add r0,r1,r0,lsr #31; bx lr
        sgnst:  asr r1,r0,#31; str r1,[r2]; bx lr
        scrub:  mov r2,#1; str r2,[r1]; mov r1,#0; mov r2,#0; bx lr
        sysarg: push {r7,lr}; asr r1,r0,#31; mov r7,#4; svc #0;
                pop {r7,lr}; bx lr
        vmsrc:  mov r1,#0x3000000; vmsr fpscr,r1; bx lr
        msrc:   mov r1,#0x13; msr cpsr_c,r1; bx lr
        feedc:  add r0,r0,#3; asr r1,r0,#31; vmsr fpscr,r1; bx lr

    sx is add r0,r0,#3 ; asr r1,r0,#31 ; bx lr.  zx is mov r1,#0 ; bx lr.

    The bug: return recovery refused r0, because its value also feeds r1
    (sx, dupc, sxsel) or because it is the caller's own r0 passing through
    (zx, sxa, kc), and the output model never returns r1 without r0, so all
    six printed as void.  kc0 reloads its argument from its spill, which the
    late pair repair took for leftover, and printed as returning 5 alone.

    The fix: when r1 is computed and read only by the RETURN, an r0 that is
    the argument in place or a value read only on its way into r1 completes
    the pair.  div7 (r1 feeds r0, an int), sgnst (r1 is stored), scrub (the
    zero -fzero-call-used-regs leaves in an r1 the body used), sysarg (r1
    set up for an svc) and vmsrc, msrc and feedc (r1 written to a system
    register) keep their answers.
-->
